From 7ab0fd99aa6974decfa84f5ed5c11d00ee810082 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Bodrov <ap.bodrov@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:54:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] netgraph/bluetooth: ng_h4, a UART (H4) HCI transport

FreeBSD has had no UART Bluetooth transport since ng_h4 was removed in
79a100e28e3c; only the USB ubt remains. This is a new node on the MPSAFE tty
API (ttyhook_register(9), as ng_tty uses): it reassembles the H4 byte stream
into HCI frames for ng_hci's drv hook and queues frames from it to the tty.
Bound with NGM_H4_NODE_SET_TTY {pid, fd} from the process holding the tty.

Tested on an Allwinner A64 (Banana Pi M64, AP6212/BCM43438A1 on uart1): after
a userland patchram load, hccontrol reset/read_bd_addr/features/buffer size,
inquiry finds a laptop, remote_name_request returns its name, and l2ping gets
5/5 echo replies (12-34 ms) over an ACL link.

Signed-off-by: Andrey Bodrov <ap.bodrov@gmail.com>
